Alphabet Inc. (GOOGL) — Q4 2024 Earnings Preview
Prepared: January 8, 2025

EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
Alphabet is expected to report Q4 2024 earnings on January 28, 2025. Consensus estimates
point to revenue of $86.3B (+12% YoY) and EPS of $1.92.

KEY THEMES TO WATCH
1. Cloud Revenue Growth: Google Cloud is expected to maintain 25%+ growth, driven by
   AI workload adoption and Gemini integration. Key question: has the enterprise pipeline
   converted at the rate management guided in Q3?

2. Search & AI Overview: Impact of AI Overviews on search monetization. Early data suggests
   ad load within AI Overviews is improving CPCs, but some analysts worry about long-term
   query cannibalization.

3. YouTube Performance: Shorts monetization gap is narrowing vs. long-form. Management
   guided for continued improvement in Q4. NFL Sunday Ticket will contribute to subscriber growth.

4. Operating Margins: Expect continued efficiency gains from headcount optimization.
   Consensus expects operating margin of 30.2%, up from 27.5% in Q4 2023.

5. Capital Expenditure: CapEx expected at $12-13B for Q4, primarily driven by AI infrastructure.
   Full-year 2024 CapEx guidance of $48-50B. Watch for 2025 CapEx guidance.

RISKS
- Regulatory headwinds from DOJ antitrust case (remedies phase)
- FX impact: strong dollar may create ~150bps revenue headwind
- Waymo cash burn trajectory

FINANCIAL ESTIMATES (Consensus)
Revenue:       $86.3B  (vs. $86.3B prior quarter consensus)
Operating Inc: $26.8B  (margin: 31.1%)
Net Income:    $23.4B
EPS:           $1.92   (vs. $1.64 Q4 2023)

VALUATION
At current price of ~$192, GOOGL trades at 22x forward P/E, a discount to
mega-cap tech peers (MSFT 33x, AAPL 30x). The discount reflects regulatory
overhang but may narrow if Cloud growth accelerates.

RECOMMENDATION: Expect a solid quarter. Focus on 2025 guidance and any
commentary on AI monetization roadmap.
